  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1998-p23.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The \\(n\\)th triangle has \\(n^2\\) small triangles.\n\nThe number of shaded small triangles is \\(1+2+\\cdots+(n-1)\\) \\(=\\dfrac{n(n-1)}{2}.\\)\n\nFor \\(n=8,\\) the shaded fraction is \\(\\dfrac{\\frac{8\\cdot 7}{2}}{8^2}=\\dfrac{7}{16}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "At step \\(n,\\) there are \\(n^2\\) small triangles.",
        "The shaded count is \\(1+2+\\cdots+(n-1).\\)"
      ],
